formation and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Present Perfect vs. The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "  <ol><li>We use the Present Perfect tense for actions which started in the past and are still happening now OR for finished actions which have a connection to the present.</li> <li>We use the Simple Past tense for past events or actions which have no connection to the present.</li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Rule\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect</span> is used when the time period has NOT finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You've looked gorgeous ever since.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You still look gorgeous.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Past</span> is used when the time period HAS finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I had a rough week.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The week is over.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Exchanging Opinions / Asking for Clarification", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You ask for clarification when you want more details of what the other person is talking about. <br/>You can exchange opinions if you and the other person have different opinions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We often ask for clarification when we are not clear on what the other person is referring to. We ask the other person to be more specific by giving more information. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You can use questions with sentences to ask for clarification. You ask a question including a sentence within the question, like <span class=\"italic\">Don't you think it sounds a bit too intense?</span> <br/>Questions with sentences are called <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions</span> like <span class=\"italic\">Can you tell me ... ?</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Do you know if/which/what ... ?</span> to ask for clarification.<br/>An <span class=\"strong\">embedded question</span> builds on a simple question.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Simple question</span>: What are you going to do after dinner?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Embedded question</span>: Do you know what you're going to do after dinner? ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you exchange opinions and ask for clarification, you can use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">I know what you mean, but ... ?</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Don't you think ... ?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for an explanation on how to make embedded questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Embedded Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Do you know ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Do you remember ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Can you tell me ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Could you tell me ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Can you tell me why they're sad? (question in a sentence)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Don't you think it's hard to live on your own in a big city? (asking for clarification)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I know what you mean, but physical activity isn't for everyone, wouldn't you agree?  (asking for clarification)", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lonely", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without friends or company", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I spoke to a couple of people who feel lonely all the time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation about social activities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to socialize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time with others socially", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People find it hard to socialize in a big city.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "on your own", "type": "name"}, {"content": "by yourself", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's hard to live on your own in a big city.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "meaningful", "type": "name"}, {"content": "serious; important; with purpose", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've had meaningful conversations after my yoga classes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Pilates", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a system of physical exercise designed by Joseph Pilates to improve overall fitness", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I only started getting fit after I joined my Pilates class.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "world-class", "type": "name"}, {"content": "among the best in the world", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You don't have to be a world-class athlete to start a new sport.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to become interested in an activity and spend time practicing it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You don't have to be a world-class athlete to take up a new sport.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a column for a newspaper (10-14 lines) about how to meet new people. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give advice to your readers on the ways they can socialize and meet people.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of 3 social activities that you have tried to meet new people. Describe them in your article and explain why they are good.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your column aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to your partner's column and ask for clarification on the social activities they described.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about past experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about social activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for clarification about social activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my opinion on social activities.", "type": "text"}]}]}